# S06: Analytics, Forecast and Business Rules

> *«Данные сами по себе ничего не оптимизируют. Оптимизация начинается тогда, когда бизнес задаёт
> им правильный вопрос.»*

## Objective

Replace every fabricated metric with a number derived from the ledgers built in S03-S05. Answer
the owner's questions with SQL rather than in-memory JavaScript. Project stockouts against a
shift-aware demand forecast. Let an owner express IF/THEN rules that create tasks for a
responsible employee — on the cron mechanism proven in S02.

## The fabricated metrics this sprint deletes

REDA currently renders these to staff as if they were measured:

| Metric | Actual source |
| ------ | ------------- |
| `customerSatisfaction` = 90 | `performance.get.ts:389` — literal, despite `orders.feedback_rating` existing and being indexed since migration 019 |
| `foodQualityScore` = '4.7' | `:349` — literal |
| `cocktailAccuracy` = 95 | `:336` — literal |
| **`wasteReduction` = 85** | `:350` — literal |
| `responseTime` | `:324` — `avgServiceTime / 2` |
| `avgPrepTime` | `:335` — `avgServiceTime * 0.4` |

`wasteReduction` as a hardcoded constant is precisely the failure mode the article mocks. After
S05 it becomes computable from prep-batch remainders; this sprint makes it real or deletes it.

